			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Reclassify remaining refactor TODOs as DEPENDENCY\n\nThis commit updates comment markers in the Maintain binary entry point files to better reflect the nature of the remaining work.\n\nIn `Source/Library.rs` and `Source/main.rs`, the generic `TODO` comments marking the future consolidation of main logic have been changed to `DEPENDENCY`. This signals that the full migration of the main function from Library.rs to main.rs cannot proceed until certain conditions are met (likely external factors or architectural decisions elsewhere in the Land ecosystem).\n\nThis aligns with the recent refactoring (commit 394b1e0) that established the binary/library separation, and clarifies the status of remaining work in the Maintain crate.",
			"SHA": "eac0bcf761cbfe4bf204129fe605988365000d3a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-03T11:28:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				63,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Maintain/Build): Implement guard disarm mechanism to preserve modified configs\n\nThis commit introduces an \"armed\" state to the Guard RAII pattern in the Maintain build system.\n\nPreviously, the Guard would always restore the original file on drop, regardless of whether the build succeeded or failed. This meant that successful builds would have their modified configuration files (Cargo.toml, Tauri config) reverted, causing unnecessary overhead.\n\nThe changes add:\n- An `Armed` boolean field to the `Guard` struct that controls whether restoration occurs\n- A `disarm()` method to explicitly prevent restoration after successful operations\n- Modified `Drop` implementation to check `self.Armed` before restoring\n\nIn `Process.rs`, both `CargoGuard` and `ConfigGuard` are now disarmed after successful build completion, preserving the modified configuration files in place.\n\nThis ensures that successful builds leave the project in a usable state without needing to re-apply configuration changes, while still providing safety via automatic restoration on failure (panic or unexpected exit).",
			"SHA": "a12cf4f541b60e9c89d6848453a8c36eb81d76b9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T10:05:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				63,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Maintain): Restructure binary entry point with dedicated main.rs\n\nThis commit refactors the Maintain binary to follow standard Rust conventions by separating the binary entry point from the library code.\n\n- Created a new `Source/main.rs` as the binary entry point that delegates to the library's main function\n- Made the `main` function in `Source/Library.rs` public to allow external calling\n- Updated `Cargo.toml` to point to `Source/main.rs` as the binary path\n- Added TODO comments indicating future plans to fully move main logic to main.rs\n- Cleaned up unused variable warnings by prefixing unused parameters with underscore (`_config`, `_e`)\n\nThis change establishes a proper binary/library separation in the Maintain crate, eliminating the current pattern where Library.rs serves double duty as both library and binary source.",
			"SHA": "394b1e0a1913f79018201a3c378a687bf93b5e42"
		},
